---
// src/pages/legal.astro
// A single legal page: what the site is, how to treat the data, copyright and
// reuse, and privacy. Plain and short, in keeping with the rest of the site.

import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Legal | RTFP"
  description="What RTFP is, how to treat the data, copyright and reuse, and privacy."
>
  <div class="legal">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Legal</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      RTFP is an independent project that puts the platforms' DSA
      transparency reports side by side. There is no company behind it and nothing
      for sale. Nothing here is legal or professional advice.
    </p>

    <h2>The data</h2>
    <p>
      Every figure comes from a platform's own filing under the Digital Services
      Act. We load and arrange those filings and fix obvious loading faults where
      we find them, with each fix recorded in the
      <a href="/fine-print/footnotes">divergence register</a>. We do not audit the
      platforms or check that what they filed is true. The
      site and its data are provided as they are, with no warranty. If you find an error in our
      handling, <a href="https://github.com/pushkinoxt/rtfp/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">open an issue</a>
      and we will look at it.
    </p>

    <h2>Copyright and reuse</h2>
    <p>
      RTFP's own work, meaning the writing on this site and the compiled dataset, is
      licensed under
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Creative Commons BY-SA 4.0</a>.
      In short, you may use any of it for any purpose, including commercially, and
      adapt it how you wish, as long as you credit RTFP and release anything you
      build from it under the same licence. We would like to know, but
      you do not have to. The underlying filings belong to the platforms that filed
      them and are public records under the Act, so they are not ours to license.
      The <a href="https://github.com/pushkinoxt/rtfp" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source code</a>
      is public. The site is open to the Internet, so everything on it will be
      crawled by search engines and other agents, and we expect it will be used to
      train large language models and the like.
    </p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      There are no accounts and no comment fields, and the site collects no personal
      information from you directly. It sets no cookies and stores nothing on your
      device, so there is no consent banner. We use Vercel Web Analytics to count
      visits and see which pages are read. It is cookieless, records only aggregate
      figures such as the page, the referrer, an approximate location and the device
      type, and identifies visitors by a hash that resets every 24 hours, so nobody
      can be followed from one day to the next or across sites. None of it is tied to
      a person. The site is served by Vercel, whose handling of requests is covered
      by its
      <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">privacy notice</a>.
      We run no advertising, and we do not sell or share any data.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal { max-width: 70ch; }
  .legal .eyebrow {
    font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
  }
  .legal h1 { font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .legal h2 { font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 1.75rem 0 0.5rem; }
  .legal p { font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--ink-dim); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 0.85rem; }
  .legal .lead { color: var(--ink); }
  .legal a { color: var(--ink); }
</style>